OL,3,GNEWSAGrieving husband says post delays
OL,4,A'adding stress'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA recently bereaved man says ongoing
OL,7,Fpostal delays in his city have added
OL,8,Ffurther stress to dealing with his
OL,9,Fwife's sudden death.
OL,11,FRuss Brookes, 44, said his family were
OL,12,F"devastated" when his wife, Em Brookes,
OL,13,Fdied in her sleep in July, but the
OL,14,Fpostal problems in Gloucester have made
OL,15,Fmanaging essential paperwork and
OL,16,Ffinances even more difficult.
OL,18,FResidents in the city have reported
OL,19,Fsecond-class letters arriving late for
OL,20,Fmonths, with some saying important
OL,21,Fcorrespondence, including medical
OL,22,Fappointments, has been delayed.
OL,23,APub: 24-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
